; Not steps after the first: a made row with a local no pattern reads is a
; fresh unknown, a new one at each firing, so a state with it is not of fixed
; terms.  Under step every over a set store, grow's match reads (a), which is
; there from the start, and each step makes another (item ?): two rows that
; may differ.  Meeting only the matches that read a fresh row would stop after
; one, so this program's steps meet every match, until the budget is spent.
(store set)
(step every)
(budget 4)
(a)
(rule grow (read (a)) (make (item $n)))
